'' See the source's header. A parameterless string intrinsic does NOT own its
'' descriptor, so the converting 'operator let' is handed a COPY.
''
'' The assertion is that the pool result reaches fb_StrAssign -- the copy fbc makes --
'' rather than the operator directly. The broken compiler emitted
'' 'call void _ZN1UaSER8FBSTRING(@a, %N)' with %N straight off fb_CurDir.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/bare-string-intrinsic-to-udt.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_CurDir
'' EXPECT-OUT: aSER8FBSTRING(@a, @$tmp
'' EXPECT-NOT: aSER8FBSTRING(@a, %
